{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: replaced the loop of indexed scalar observations `y[n] ~ bernoulli(theta[group[n]])` with the equivalent vectorized sampling statement `y ~ bernoulli(theta[group])`. This preserves the same Bernoulli likelihood while making the protected observation a single top-level data variable observed exactly once. No data changes were required.
","model_safe_stan":"// ForestDB translation: Biases from Noise
data {
  int<lower=1> G;
  int<lower=1> N;
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=G> group;
  array[N] int<lower=0, upper=1> y;
}
parameters {
  real<lower=0> alpha;
  real<lower=0> beta;
  vector<lower=0, upper=1>[G] theta;
}
model {
  alpha ~ gamma(2, 1);
  beta ~ gamma(2, 1);
  theta ~ beta(alpha, beta);
  y ~ bernoulli(theta[group]);
}
generated quantities {
  real population_mean = alpha / (alpha + beta);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"G":2,"N":4,"group":[1,1,2,1],"y":[0,1,1,1]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
